<h2 class="prose">What this leaves out</h2>
<p class="prose">A perfectly straight, centrally loaded, prismatic strut. A real one is none of those, and the codes handle it with a column curve that folds initial bow, residual stress and eccentricity into a reduction factor rather than with the Euler load and a factor of safety. This is the calculation that shows what is happening; a code check is what a drawing is signed against.</p>

